1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,662
A workflow becomes useful when it can compute a value, remember it, choose

2
00:00:05,662 --> 00:00:07,527
a path, and repeat a step.

3
00:00:07,527 --> 00:00:12,480
In this video, we'll look at expressions, variables, branches, and loops in the

4
00:00:12,480 --> 00:00:15,860
Workflows module, and at how to extend them in code.

5
00:00:20,460 --> 00:00:25,341
Many settings are expressions, evaluated each time the activity runs.

6
00:00:25,341 --> 00:00:31,525
In If/Else, For Each, Set Variable and a few others, you choose each expression's syntax.

7
00:00:31,525 --> 00:00:36,406
Literal means the text is the value itself, Liquid is a template, and

8
00:00:36,406 --> 00:00:39,400
JavaScript runs in the Scripting module.

9
00:00:40,150 --> 00:00:43,579
The activity stores the expression with its syntax.

10
00:00:43,579 --> 00:00:48,391
This If/Else condition could be the Literal true, a Liquid comparison on a

11
00:00:48,391 --> 00:00:51,339
property, or a JavaScript test on an input.

12
00:00:51,339 --> 00:00:55,730
A JavaScript result must already have the type the setting expects.

13
00:00:57,380 --> 00:01:00,555
This workflow counts the coffees in a list.

14
00:01:00,555 --> 00:01:05,221
Double-click Each item, a For Each activity, to open its settings.

15
00:01:05,221 --> 00:01:10,080
Its Items setting uses the Literal syntax, so the list is plain text.

16
00:01:10,611 --> 00:01:13,098
Check the item is an If/Else activity.

17
00:01:13,098 --> 00:01:18,071
Its Condition is a JavaScript expression, and the property function reads the item

18
00:01:18,071 --> 00:01:19,541
that the loop is on.

19
00:01:20,022 --> 00:01:24,933
Write the summary is a Set Variable activity that uses Liquid, and reads

20
00:01:24,933 --> 00:01:27,577
the variables as Workflow.Variables.

21
00:01:27,577 --> 00:01:32,362
Each expression has its own syntax, so one workflow can mix all three.

22
00:01:39,350 --> 00:01:44,000
The Available data tab lists what the expressions of an activity can read:

23
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:48,533
variables, values from earlier activities, global values, and functions.

24
00:01:48,533 --> 00:01:51,090
Click one to insert it in the setting.

25
00:01:55,370 --> 00:01:59,966
Variables are declared in the Variables tab of the workflow panel.

26
00:01:59,966 --> 00:02:05,648
Each has a name, a type, an optional default value, and the Input and Output flags.

27
00:02:05,648 --> 00:02:09,670
Here, summary is an Output, so the Run dialog reports it.

28
00:02:11,270 --> 00:02:15,941
The types are Text, Number, Yes or no, Date and time, Object, List,

29
00:02:15,941 --> 00:02:17,733
Content item, and Any.

30
00:02:17,733 --> 00:02:21,317
Setting a variable converts the value to its type.

31
00:02:21,317 --> 00:02:26,244
Set Variable faults the workflow when the value does not convert, but a

32
00:02:26,244 --> 00:02:28,740
script logs the error by default.

33
00:02:29,490 --> 00:02:35,924
In JavaScript, the variable function reads a variable, and the setVariable function writes it.

34
00:02:35,924 --> 00:02:38,819
In Liquid, Workflow.Variables reads it.

35
00:02:38,819 --> 00:02:44,030
The Set Variable activity stores the result of an expression in a variable.

36
00:02:44,780 --> 00:02:46,894
Some activities produce outputs.

37
00:02:46,894 --> 00:02:50,789
On the Outputs tab, Store in binds an output, such as the Result

38
00:02:50,789 --> 00:02:54,740
of a Script, to a variable that the activities after it can read.

39
00:02:58,940 --> 00:03:04,633
Each activity has outcomes, and a transition connects an outcome to the next activity.

40
00:03:04,633 --> 00:03:08,470
If/Else evaluates its Condition and takes True or False.

41
00:03:08,470 --> 00:03:12,740
A Script activity lists its own outcomes in Available Outcomes.

42
00:03:13,490 --> 00:03:16,677
The script calls setOutcome with one of those names.

43
00:03:16,677 --> 00:03:20,577
Here, the outcome is the value of a state variable, so each state

44
00:03:20,577 --> 00:03:22,610
can lead to its own activities.

45
00:03:24,310 --> 00:03:28,779
On the canvas, Check the item shows its two outcomes, True and False,

46
00:03:28,779 --> 00:03:31,580
and each one has a transition of its own.

47
00:03:32,062 --> 00:03:35,903
By default, an outcome follows only its first transition.

48
00:03:35,903 --> 00:03:41,512
The Workflow tab can set Outcomes with several transitions to Follow every transition,

49
00:03:41,512 --> 00:03:44,499
which runs every branch in the order added.

50
00:03:44,499 --> 00:03:47,182
A separate video covers Fork and Join.

51
00:03:51,382 --> 00:03:53,941
Three activities repeat part of a workflow.

52
00:03:53,941 --> 00:03:57,597
For Each goes through a list, For Loop counts from a start value

53
00:03:57,597 --> 00:04:01,462
to an end value, and While Loop repeats while its condition is true.

54
00:04:02,212 --> 00:04:05,261
Each loop has two outcomes, Iterate and Done.

55
00:04:05,261 --> 00:04:10,043
Connect Iterate to the activities to repeat, connect the last of them back

56
00:04:10,043 --> 00:04:13,152
to the loop, and connect Done to what follows.

57
00:04:13,902 --> 00:04:18,250
Each pass of For Each sets the property named by Looping Variable and

58
00:04:18,250 --> 00:04:20,686
the last result, then takes Iterate.

59
00:04:20,686 --> 00:04:23,237
When the items run out, it takes Done.

60
00:04:23,237 --> 00:04:27,992
For Loop works the same way with a number, and its To value is not included.

61
00:04:29,640 --> 00:04:33,086
Here, Iterate leads from Each item to Check the item.

62
00:04:33,086 --> 00:04:37,466
Its True outcome leads to Count the coffee, and that activity and the

63
00:04:37,466 --> 00:04:40,211
False outcome both lead back to the loop.

64
00:04:40,211 --> 00:04:42,430
Done leads to Write the summary.

65
00:04:42,899 --> 00:04:46,086
Run, in the toolbar, starts the published version.

66
00:04:46,086 --> 00:04:50,753
The dialog reports the status of the instance and the output variables, here

67
00:04:50,753 --> 00:04:52,859
the summary the workflow wrote.

68
00:04:53,360 --> 00:04:55,807
Open the instance to see what happened.

69
00:04:55,807 --> 00:04:59,941
The path it ran is highlighted, and a badge on the repeated activities

70
00:04:59,941 --> 00:05:01,900
shows how many times they ran.

71
00:05:02,421 --> 00:05:05,841
The Variables tab shows the values this instance has:

72
00:05:05,841 --> 00:05:08,681
the number of coffees and the summary text.

73
00:05:12,881 --> 00:05:18,841
A module adds a syntax by implementing IWorkflowExpressionProvider, with a name, a display

74
00:05:18,841 --> 00:05:22,131
name, and an editor language as static members.

75
00:05:22,131 --> 00:05:27,471
AddWorkflowExpressionProvider registers it, and it appears in the syntax select.

76
00:05:28,221 --> 00:05:36,338
An activity evaluates its expressions through IWorkflowExpressionManager, which finds the provider for each expression's syntax.

77
00:05:36,338 --> 00:05:40,821
If/Else evaluates its Condition this way, and returns True or False.

78
00:05:41,571 --> 00:05:46,611
The functions that JavaScript expressions call come from global method providers.

79
00:05:46,611 --> 00:05:51,188
Only the Script activity passes setOutcome, as a method scoped to its own

80
00:05:51,188 --> 00:05:55,591
evaluation, which is why the other built-in activities do not have it.

81
00:05:56,341 --> 00:06:00,745
The JavaScript engine sets no time or statement limit by default, so you

82
00:06:00,745 --> 00:06:02,609
can set one on its options.

83
00:06:02,609 --> 00:06:06,731
A script that reaches a limit faults the workflow at that activity.

84
00:06:07,481 --> 00:06:12,384
Any other script error is logged, and the activity goes on with a default value.

85
00:06:12,384 --> 00:06:17,971
To stop there instead, check Fault the workflow on script errors in the workflow's settings.

86
00:06:19,971 --> 00:06:25,477
Expressions compute, variables remember, outcomes choose a path, and loops repeat it.

87
00:06:25,477 --> 00:06:27,051
Thanks for watching.

